title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/kmtinterparty.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The KMT can decide to strengthen ties with other factions to garner more support.

- @communists: Strengthen our bonds with the Chinese Communist Party, which will earn us favors from the Soviets.
- @localwarlords: Strengthen our bonds with Guangxi, Yunnan and Guizhou's warlords.
- @kmt_alone: The SPD can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@communists
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources. [? if cpc_civil_war = 1 : The Kuomintang and the Communist Party have split permanently. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; cpc_relations += 8; east_realtions += 1;

Cooperating with the CPC on our United Front is accepted by many in the party, with the exception of the Right.

@localwarlords
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; gxc_relations += 7; yun_relations += 7; gui_relations += 7; rural_kmt -= 3;

Making friends with warlords do not reflect well on us. Especially to our supporters.

@kmt_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other factions at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
